  "instructions": [
    "Heat vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium heat.",
    "Add katsuramuki-cut carrots and cook until they start to soften, about 5 minutes.",
    "Add dried dates, sesame oil, sesame seeds, honey, rice wine vinegar, sugar, salt, and black pepper.",
    "Cook for an additional 10 minutes, or until the carrots are tender and the sauce has thickened.",
    "Stir in thinly sliced green onions and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Serve the Jewelled Korean Date Jorim warm or at room temperature."
